# TP4 (four Sparks): copy to cluster.env (in the repo root or config/) on every box, or pass @<file>. ./gr8 glm53
# parses it (KEY=value lines; no $ expansion). The command line wins over it, and it wins over the environment.
# Every box must end up with the same cluster options; per-box values (paths, PROXY_CPU) may differ. KNOBS.md lists all.

# The boxes' LAN addresses, in rank order. The first is the head: the front end and the shim run there. Every box lists
# the same addresses in the same order.
PEERS=10.0.0.1,10.0.0.2,10.0.0.3,10.0.0.4
# Or let mentat find the boxes (the default when PEERS is unset): MENTAT=localhost and TP=4.
#MENTAT=localhost
#TP=4

# A prepared pack directory (scripts/build_packs.sh's OUT_DIR, with the drafter packs and a tokenizer/ directory or
# MODEL_DIR): every rank's manifest must be there. A shared mount is fine.
MODEL=/data/packs
# This box's local disk. The first boot copies this box's shard of the model set there; later boots read it.
MODEL_CACHE=/opt/g6/cache
# The tokenizer files, when MODEL has no tokenizer/ directory (the TR3 checkpoint directory has all four).
#MODEL_DIR=/opt/models/GLM-5.3-EXL3-TR3-3.25bpw

# Working directory on this box: bin/, out/, s2/, serve/, run/. Defaults to the repo checkout. Nodes without the CUDA
# toolkit: build with BUNDLE_LIBS=1 (scripts/build.sh); the engine finds cuBLAS in bin/lib.
G6_HOME=/opt/g6

# CPU core for this rank's fabric proxy thread (GB10 has 20 cores, 0-19).
PROXY_CPU=19

# HTTP port of the OpenAI-compatible front end on the head.
PORT=8100

# Optional. Each box finds its two RoCE v2 addresses itself (rail 0 is the lower). Set these to pin them: the address of
# every rank on fabric rail 1 and rail 2.
#IPS=10.0.1.1,10.0.1.2,10.0.1.3,10.0.1.4
#IPS2=10.0.2.1,10.0.2.2,10.0.2.3,10.0.2.4

# Optional. Any launch knob (KNOBS.md), for example the KV pool:
#CAP=393216

# Only for the deprecated ssh launchers (./gr8 glm53 --ssh up), which run everything from the head over ssh and need
# HOSTS (ssh names), IPS, IPS2 and MODEL_DIR. ./gr8 glm53 up reads HOSTS as PEERS when PEERS is unset.
#HOSTS="node1 node2 node3 node4"
